From: kmorph bootc experiment <kmorph@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] multikernel: Set pcifront direct access before any bus is adopted

mk_pcifront_host_fenced() returned early when mk_pcifront_buses was
empty.  A backup has no PCI buses of its own at boot; the host's buses
are described in /chosen/multikernel,pci-buses and are added lazily by
mk_pcifront_host_bus() when a function is adopted.  On an arm64
takeover the fence therefore left mk_pcifront_direct_access false, and
every mk_pcifront_adopt_function() returned -EPERM.  No device moved:
the successor lost its disk, network and console.

Set the flag at the fence regardless; the buses and their ECAM windows
are picked up as each function is adopted.

Tested on an arm64 Fedora bootc guest under QEMU/KVM: all three virtio
functions (block, net, serial) are adopted after the fence.

diff --git a/kernel/multikernel/pcifront.c b/kernel/multikernel/pcifront.c
--- a/kernel/multikernel/pcifront.c
+++ b/kernel/multikernel/pcifront.c
@@ -147,8 +147,7 @@ void mk_pcifront_host_fenced(void)
 	struct mk_pcifront_bus *fb;
 	bool direct = false;
 
-	if (READ_ONCE(mk_pcifront_direct_access) ||
-	    list_empty(&mk_pcifront_buses))
+	if (READ_ONCE(mk_pcifront_direct_access))
 		return;
 	WRITE_ONCE(mk_pcifront_direct_access, true);
 
